+## Scratch storage
 
-In this fork's AD output, the SCS-MP2 and same/opposite-spin diagnostic lines
-are legacy placeholders because that path does not populate spin components.
-Use the ordinary `E(MP2)` and total gradient for this benchmark, not those SCS
-diagnostics. The plain PySCF driver does compute the spin components.
+Both submission scripts set:
+
+```bash
+SCRATCH_DIR="/resnick/scratch/$USER/dcmp-ooc/$SLURM_JOB_ID"
+export TMPDIR="$SCRATCH_DIR" PYSCF_TMPDIR="$SCRATCH_DIR"
+```
+
+[Caltech's storage documentation](https://www.hpc.caltech.edu/docs/documentation/storage.html)
+identifies `/resnick/scratch` as all-NVMe VAST storage, with no separate high-I/O
+tier. This is the documented high-performance scratch choice. The inspected
+Ice Lake node records do not advertise scheduler-guaranteed local scratch.
+No claim of benchmark-proven optimal I/O is made.
+
+Caltech documents a 20 TB default scratch quota and purging after 14 days
+without access. The scripts retain their scratch files for inspection; move
+anything needed long-term to project storage. SLURM output and program results
+remain in this calculation directory. No automatic cleanup or resubmission is
+added.
+
+## Threads and timings
+
+Native OpenMP uses 16 workers. BLAS pools remain at one thread except that the
+existing scoped SciPy pool uses 16 during DF setup and the final attachment
+pullback. The latter is now just geometry-cotangent routing: the actual DF
+integral derivative work is included in the SCF and MP2 pullback timings.
+Consequently, individual DF/reverse timings are not directly comparable to
+the old in-core phase breakdown. Total time includes disk DF construction.
+
+The plain PySCF run computes energy only, while the AD run also differentiates
+it. Their HDF5 layouts may differ. Do not interpret their total-time ratio as
+an isolated comparison of DF algorithms.
+
+## Validation
+
+The small water-dimer check is self-contained in
+`/resnick/groups/sharmagroup/bkhou/src/pyscfad/benchmarks/dcmp-ooc-check`.
+It compares the original in-core phase-split AD driver against the modified
+out-of-core AD driver and plain PySCF, using def2-SVP / weigend, two frozen
+orbitals, and all 18 coordinate-gradient components. Production dCMP inputs
+retain cc-pVTZ / cc-pVTZ-JKFIT and 24 frozen orbitals.
+
+Validation job **5818204** completed successfully on Ice Lake node
+`hpc-53-08` on 2026-10-31. Maximum differences were 3.41e-13 Eh for in-core
+versus out-of-core AD energy, 2.43e-14 Eh/bohr across the full gradient, and
+2.27e-13 Eh for plain PySCF versus AD energy. Evidence is in the validation
+folder's `verification.json`, `slurm-5818204.out`, and three calculation logs.
+No calculations ran on a login node. The full dCMP production jobs have not
+been submitted as part of this input edit.
+
+Original inputs and the complete edit diff are saved in that validation
+folder as `original_inputs/` and `input_changes.diff`.
